WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:17.520
This lesson maps every one of the eleven current Week Two Moodle links: eight video demonstrations and three EMSWorld articles. It teaches their central ideas in new words; it is not a subtitle dump, video replacement or official school presentation.
本课对应当前Moodle第2周全部11个链接：8个视频演示和3篇EMSWorld文章。内容用原创表述讲解核心概念，不是字幕堆积、视频替代品或学校官方课件。

00:00:17.520 --> 00:00:32.208
The first four demonstrations show i-gel placement, a proposed suction add-on, a King LTS-D device and rigid-tip pharyngeal suction. Compare each with the current BCEHS procedure and the actual skill your instructor assigns.
前四个演示分别展示i-gel置入、附加吸引方法、King LTS-D器械及硬质头咽部吸引。须逐一与当前BCEHS规程及教师实际安排的技能比较。

00:00:32.208 --> 00:00:48.096
The intubation and Melker videos show advanced procedures; the CPAP videos show a Queensland service and a specific Rescuer 8700 product. They explain what those sources demonstrate, not what every BC PCP may perform.
气管插管和Melker视频展示高级操作；CPAP视频展示昆士兰服务方案及特定Rescuer 8700产品。它们说明来源展示了什么，不代表每名BC PCP都可执行。

00:00:48.096 --> 00:01:04.152
The final three articles revisit acute PE, COPD exacerbation and undifferentiated breathlessness. Use them to practise clinical reasoning, then cross-check any threshold, intervention or scope statement against the current local guideline.
最后三篇文章重看急性肺栓塞、COPD急性加重及未分化呼吸困难。可用来练习临床推理，但任何阈值、干预或权限都要再核对本地现行指引。

00:01:04.152 --> 00:01:16.032
A video can be technically clear yet still use a different device, country, protocol revision or provider licence. Accurate observation is not the same as local authorization.
视频可以拍得很清楚，却使用不同器械、国家、规程版本或从业者权限。看清操作不等于取得本地操作授权。

00:01:16.032 --> 00:01:29.664
Ask who produced the demonstration, what device model is shown, and whether it is a service training video, manufacturer marketing, or a general skills clip. Those categories carry different evidentiary weight.
先看演示者、器械型号，以及它属于服务培训、制造商宣传还是通用技能视频。这些类别的证据分量并不相同。

00:01:29.664 --> 00:01:45.168
For BC PCP field practice, the current BCEHS handbook, applicable PCP procedure, actual school station and your instructor’s sign-off govern. For a device-specific detail, use the exact approved device instructions as well.
BC PCP实务以当前BCEHS手册、适用PCP规程、学校实际训练站及教师签核为准。器械专属细节还须看对应获批说明书。

00:01:45.168 --> 00:02:02.016
For airway support, the endpoint is an effective, reassessed breath: appropriate chest rise, airflow, patient response and available monitoring. A tube or mask that is merely in place is not proof of effective oxygenation or ventilation.
气道支持的终点是有效且经复评的呼吸：适当胸廓起伏、气流、患者反应及可用监测。管子或面罩仅仅放上去，不证明氧合或通气有效。

00:02:02.016 --> 00:02:15.168
The BCEHS Professional Practice i-gel video demonstrates preparation, insertion, fixation and troubleshooting. Its useful learning point is that placement has to be followed by a real ventilation check.
BCEHS Professional Practice的i-gel视频演示准备、置入、固定及排错。可迁移的重点是：置入后必须真实核查通气效果。

00:02:15.168 --> 00:02:29.880
Current PR08 requires prior ability to ventilate with a bag-valve mask and lists airway obstruction, active vomiting and other exclusions. The SGA is a staged option, not a shortcut around a blocked airway.
当前PR08要求先能用球囊面罩通气，并列明气道阻塞、活动性呕吐等排除情况。声门上气道是分阶段选择，不是绕过阻塞的捷径。

00:02:29.880 --> 00:02:42.936
The current procedure describes the i-gel rather than the separate King device shown in another video. Confirm the correct school-supplied size and model; do not mix manufacturers’ parts, cuff assumptions or holders.
当前规程描述的是i-gel，而不是另一视频中的King器械。须确认学校提供的型号与尺寸，不要混用不同厂商零件、套囊概念或固定器。

00:02:42.936 --> 00:02:56.664
If placement fails, return to effective BVM with the required filter and seek help. If placement appears successful, continue to reassess after every movement or change in patient condition.
置入失败时，按要求使用过滤器恢复有效BVM并求援。即使看似成功，每次搬动或患者状态变化后也要继续复评。

00:02:56.664 --> 00:03:13.248
The BCEHS suction video describes a nasogastric tube and historic pandemic-era equipment. Do not reproduce that technique from the video: PCP pharyngeal suction is limited by current PR27 and does not authorize gastric intubation.
BCEHS吸引视频讲到鼻胃管及疫情时期器械。不能照视频复制该技术：PCP咽部吸引受当前PR27限制，也不授权插胃管。

00:03:13.248 --> 00:03:28.656
PR27 specifies the supplied Resus Pack catheter, a package-based depth measurement with a two-centimetre allowance, lubricant and a clear depth mark. The device-specific step must be learned on the actual supervised trainer.
PR27规定使用Resus Pack随附导管，按包装测量并增加2厘米、润滑并清楚标记深度。器械专属动作须在实际训练模型上学习。

00:03:28.656 --> 00:03:48.096
The procedure uses 80 mmHg and says not generally to exceed 160 mmHg. Stop when fluid clears or after 15 to 20 seconds without fluid; continuous suction may harm. These limits belong to this procedure, not every suction task.
该规程使用80毫米汞柱，一般不超过160毫米汞柱。液体清除或15至20秒无液体时应停止；持续吸引可能造成伤害。这些限制只属于该流程，不适用于所有吸引操作。

00:03:48.096 --> 00:04:04.512
Current PR08 and PR27 require removal of the i-gel during active vomiting or difficult ventilation after vomiting, followed by oropharyngeal clearance and restoration of effective support. Never let the old video override this branch.
当前PR08及PR27要求：i-gel在位时活动性呕吐，或呕吐后通气困难，须取出装置、清理口咽并恢复有效支持。不能让旧视频覆盖这一处理分支。

00:04:04.512 --> 00:04:19.584
The WCTC Fire and EMS skills video presents a rigid-tip oral suction example for vomit, blood and secretions. It emphasizes maintaining sight of the tip and recognizing that a rigid catheter can cause trauma.
WCTC Fire and EMS技能视频用硬质吸引头清除呕吐物、血液及分泌物，并强调保持尖端可见及认识到硬管可能造成创伤。

00:04:19.584 --> 00:04:33.096
Its advice about use in a moving ambulance belongs to that US educational demonstration. Do not turn it into a BC service rule without a current local source; instead learn the assigned school safety standard.
视频关于行驶救护车中使用的建议属于美国教学演示。没有当前本地来源时，不应把它当作BC服务规定；应学习学校安排的安全标准。

00:04:33.096 --> 00:04:46.800
Suction is effective only if the airway is cleared and ventilation resumes. The screen’s depiction of suction, the sound of the pump or an empty canister does not establish that the patient is now breathing adequately.
只有气道被清理且通气恢复，吸引才算有效。画面显示正在吸、泵有声音或收集罐为空，都不能证明患者现已呼吸充分。

00:04:46.800 --> 00:04:59.976
The technique, suction level, insertion limits and infection-control setup must match the exact school equipment and current procedure. Rehearse on a trainer with the instructor watching and correcting your hand position.
技术、负压、置入限制及感染控制设置都必须符合学校实际器械及现行规程。应在模型上演练，由教师观察并纠正手位。

00:04:59.976 --> 00:05:13.296
The Live Action Safety overview is a King Systems product demonstration of the LTS-D, including cuffs, ventilation openings, an alternate suction or gastric-access lumen, and device-specific positioning.
Live Action Safety视频是King Systems产品演示，讲解LTS-D套囊、通气口、额外吸引或胃通道及器械专属定位。

00:05:13.296 --> 00:05:27.696
The video’s cuff volumes, pressure advice, size ranges and gastric-tube claims belong to that manufacturer’s device and training context. They are not transferable instructions for i-gel or the school’s PCP airway station.
视频中的套囊容量、压力建议、尺寸范围及胃管说明，属于该厂商器械与培训情境，不能转用到i-gel或学校PCP气道站。

00:05:27.696 --> 00:05:44.616
Current BCEHS PR08 names the i-gel as the local supraglottic airway procedure and sets conditions, contraindications, prior BVM confirmation and securement. A general resemblance between devices does not expand the approved equipment list.
当前BCEHS PR08规定本地声门上气道流程使用i-gel，并设定适用条件、禁忌、先行BVM确认及固定要求。器械外形相似不代表获批器械清单扩大。

00:05:44.616 --> 00:05:59.304
For the exam, be able to state what a supraglottic device aims to accomplish and why its seal is not equivalent to a cuffed tracheal tube. For hands-on practice, use only the device and sequence specified by the instructor.
考试时应能说明声门上装置的目标，以及为何其密封不等同套囊气管导管。实操时只使用教师指定的器械及流程。

00:05:59.304 --> 00:06:15.552
The Moodle item named “Endotracheal Intubation” links to a clip titled “Endotracheal Ventilation.” It shows laryngoscopy, tube placement and auscultation in a general training context; it does not establish a BC PCP procedure.
Moodle名为“Endotracheal Intubation”的项目链接到标题为“Endotracheal Ventilation”的视频。它在通用培训情境中展示喉镜、置管及听诊，不构成BC PCP操作规程。

00:06:15.552 --> 00:06:30.552
The Melker video is a product-specific emergency cricothyrotomy demonstration using a wire and dilator catheter set. Current BCEHS PR22 instead defines its own age-specific techniques and provider scope.
Melker视频是特定产品的紧急环甲膜切开演示，采用导丝及扩张导管套件。当前BCEHS PR22另行规定按年龄选择的技术与从业者权限。

00:06:30.552 --> 00:06:47.472
BCEHS B01 places intubation within the ACP pathway, and PR22 applies to ACP and higher. These videos are useful for recognizing what advanced escalation involves, not for unsupervised rehearsal or claiming PCP authorization.
BCEHS B01把气管插管列入ACP路径，PR22适用于ACP及以上。这些视频可帮助理解高级升级处理，不适用于无监督演练或声称PCP获权。

00:06:47.472 --> 00:07:04.104
Your PCP learning task is to recognize deteriorating oxygenation or ventilation, continue authorized basic support, summon appropriate resources early and communicate the patient’s response. Do not delay BVM while discussing an advanced procedure.
PCP学习重点是识别氧合或通气恶化、继续获授权的基础支持、尽早请求适当资源，并报告患者反应。讨论高级操作时不能延误BVM。

00:07:04.104 --> 00:07:19.056
The Queensland Ambulance Service clip introduces a disposable CPAP design and explains how oxygen flow through a valve creates continuous pressure. That helps visualize the mechanism, not the current BC service protocol.
Queensland Ambulance Service视频介绍一次性CPAP装置，并说明氧气经阀门产生持续压力的原理。这有助于理解机制，但不是当前BC服务规程。

00:07:19.056 --> 00:07:33.840
The video was made for an Australian service rollout in 2013. Its device, flow rates, pressure escalation, eligibility and documentation cannot be transplanted into the BCEHS procedure or a different mask.
该视频为2013年澳大利亚服务推广制作。它的装置、流量、压力递增、适用条件及记录要求，不能直接搬到BCEHS规程或其他面罩上。

00:07:33.840 --> 00:07:50.952
CPAP provides continuous positive pressure while the patient breathes; it does not squeeze a breath into the lungs. If respiratory drive, tidal volume or consciousness is failing, the patient needs an authorized ventilation pathway, not CPAP as a substitute.
患者自主呼吸时，CPAP提供持续正压；它不会把一次呼吸挤入肺部。如果呼吸驱动、潮气量或意识正在衰退，患者需要获授权的通气路径，不能用CPAP代替。

00:07:50.952 --> 00:08:05.952
Use the mechanism to understand why a mask leak, intolerance, vomiting, low pressure or deterioration matters. Then apply the current BCEHS PR09 criteria, contraindications and reassessment instructions.
可用该机制理解面罩漏气、不耐受、呕吐、低血压或恶化为何重要；之后必须按当前BCEHS PR09的适用条件、禁忌及复评要求操作。

00:08:05.952 --> 00:08:20.832
The Rescuer 8700 demonstration shows a silicone mask, adjustable headgear, pressure control, a medication port and an anti-suffocation valve. These are product features, not universal CPAP components.
Rescuer 8700演示展示硅胶面罩、可调头带、压力控制、药物接口及防窒息阀。这些是产品特点，不是所有CPAP装置的通用构造。

00:08:20.832 --> 00:08:33.912
Its instructions about flow, pressure adjustment and medication delivery apply to that product and its own instructions for use. Do not infer the school’s current device or treatment settings from a product video title.
视频中的流量、压力调节及药物给药说明只适用于该产品及其说明书。不能从产品视频标题推断学校当前使用的装置或治疗设置。

00:08:33.912 --> 00:08:49.368
The anti-suffocation valve is a device safeguard; it does not correct respiratory arrest, hypoventilation, reduced consciousness or aspiration risk. The person still requires continuous assessment and a backup plan.
防窒息阀是器械安全功能，不能纠正呼吸骤停、通气不足、意识下降或误吸风险。患者仍须持续评估并准备后备方案。

00:08:49.368 --> 00:09:03.552
Treat all pressure and interface changes as device-specific. In class, inspect the exact approved system with your instructor and state the current PR09 patient criteria before rehearsing its application.
所有压力与接口设置都视为器械专属。在课堂上应与教师检查准确获批的系统，并在演练前说出当前PR09患者条件。

00:09:03.552 --> 00:09:21.240
Current BCEHS PR09 applies to PCPs with AIME CPAP training and higher; prior CliniCall consultation is recommended for PCPs. The patient must be at least thirteen, awake, able to follow commands and able to maintain an open airway.
当前BCEHS PR09适用于完成AIME CPAP培训的PCP及以上；建议PCP使用前先联系CliniCall。患者须年满13岁、清醒、能遵从指令并能维持气道开放。

00:09:21.240 --> 00:09:38.304
The listed respiratory-distress pattern includes respiratory rate above twenty-four per minute, oxygen saturation below ninety-four percent on supplemental oxygen, and accessory-muscle use. Apply all current criteria together rather than choosing one number.
所列呼吸窘迫模式包括呼吸频率高于每分钟24次、补充氧后血氧低于94%，以及辅助呼吸肌参与。应综合当前全部条件，不能只挑一个数字。

00:09:38.304 --> 00:09:58.848
PR09 excludes age twelve and under, reduced consciousness or inability to follow commands, respiratory arrest or hypoventilation, inability to fit the mask, vomiting or aspiration risk, traumatic distress, tracheostomy, suspected pneumothorax and systolic pressure below ninety.
PR09排除12岁及以下、意识下降或不能遵嘱、呼吸骤停或通气不足、面罩无法贴合、呕吐或误吸风险、创伤性呼吸窘迫、气管切开、疑似气胸及收缩压低于90。

00:09:58.848 --> 00:10:17.400
Explain the treatment and obtain consent; position and monitor as directed; fit and reassess the mask; follow the current device chart and PR09 ceilings. If the patient worsens, stop treating the device as the goal and move to the authorized backup pathway.
解释治疗并取得同意；按要求摆位及监测；贴合面罩并复评；遵循当前设备图表及PR09上限。患者恶化时，不要把设备当成目标，应转入获授权的后备路径。

00:10:17.400 --> 00:10:34.056
The school-linked 2015 EMSWorld article uses a postoperative trauma case to teach why recent surgery, injury and reduced mobility matter. Its population statistics and US-specific treatment statements are historical, not current BC instructions.
学校链接的2015年EMSWorld文章使用术后创伤案例，说明近期手术、损伤及活动减少为何重要。其人口统计和美国治疗说法均属历史资料，不是当前BC指令。

00:10:34.056 --> 00:10:47.784
A pulmonary embolus obstructs pulmonary blood flow. The resulting dead-space and gas-exchange problem can combine with increased pulmonary vascular resistance and right-ventricular strain, reducing effective forward flow.
肺栓子阻塞肺循环血流。由此产生的无效腔及气体交换问题，可能与肺血管阻力增加、右心室负荷上升同时出现，降低有效前向血流。

00:10:47.784 --> 00:11:07.416
Ask about recent surgery, hospitalization, reduced mobility, prior venous thromboembolism, malignancy, pregnancy or hormonal change. Sudden dyspnea, pleuritic pain, cough, syncope or hypotension can raise concern, but no one finding proves PE.
询问近期手术、住院、活动受限、既往静脉血栓栓塞、恶性肿瘤、妊娠或激素变化。突然呼吸困难、胸膜性疼痛、咳嗽、晕厥或低血压可增加疑虑，但任何单一发现都不能证明肺栓塞。

00:11:07.416 --> 00:11:26.568
Current BCEHS B06 calls for supportive care, oxygen as required, monitoring and rapid conveyance; unstable patients need a transport plan that preserves resuscitation capability. Do not use an old article’s scoring table or fluid/drug plan as a PCP order.
当前BCEHS B06要求支持治疗、按需给氧、监测及快速转运；不稳定患者需制定能保留复苏能力的转运方案。不能把旧文章评分表或液体、药物方案当作PCP医嘱。

00:11:26.568 --> 00:11:41.544
The 2015 EMSWorld COPD article illustrates a useful diagnostic habit: compare with the patient’s usual function and include competing causes such as heart failure, pulmonary embolism, pneumonia and pneumothorax.
2015年EMSWorld COPD文章展示了有用的诊断习惯：与患者平时状态比较，并考虑心衰、肺栓塞、肺炎及气胸等其他病因。

00:11:41.544 --> 00:11:55.680
An exacerbation is an acute change from baseline, often increased breathlessness, more frequent or severe cough, or a change in sputum. A familiar diagnosis does not rule out a second new emergency.
急性加重是相对基线的急性变化，常见呼吸困难加重、咳嗽更频繁或更严重、痰量或性状改变。既往诊断熟悉，不代表排除新的并发急症。

00:11:55.680 --> 00:12:13.680
Current BCEHS B05 describes COPD as primarily a ventilation problem and warns that critical hypercarbia may occur even when the respiratory rate looks high. Watch the trend: falling consciousness, decreasing rate and shrinking tidal volumes are red flags.
当前BCEHS B05把COPD主要描述为通气问题，并警示呼吸频率看似较高时仍可能出现严重高碳酸血症。要看趋势：意识下降、频率降低、潮气量变小都是危险信号。

00:12:13.680 --> 00:12:32.232
B05 says to use the patient’s usual saturation when readily known, titrate to the current 88-92 percent target, and never withhold oxygen from an acutely short-of-breath patient. Avoid exertion during movement, convey early and follow current medication scope.
B05要求在容易获得时参考患者平时血氧，按当前88%至92%目标滴定；绝不能对急性气促患者扣留氧气。搬动时避免增加活动量，尽早转运并遵循当前药物权限。

00:12:32.232 --> 00:12:43.992
The 2009 Shortness of Breath article connects respiratory mechanics with cardiac causes and demonstrates that dyspnea can occur with myocardial ischemia even when chest pain is absent.
2009年《Shortness of Breath》文章把呼吸力学与心脏病因联系起来，并指出即使没有胸痛，心肌缺血也可表现为呼吸困难。

00:12:43.992 --> 00:12:59.136
The article also surveys COPD, asthma-like wheeze, infection and heart failure, but its old statistics, labels and treatment examples should not be memorized as current practice. Use current BCEHS pages for actual clinical direction.
文章还讨论COPD、类似哮喘的喘鸣、感染及心衰，但旧统计、标签及治疗例子不能当作当前实践背诵。实际临床方向应看当前BCEHS页面。

00:12:59.136 --> 00:13:13.224
Build a time course: abrupt or progressive, at rest or exertion, positional, infection-linked or trauma-linked. Ask what is normal for this person and what changed before selecting a cause.
先建立时间线：突然还是渐进、静息还是活动时、是否与体位、感染或创伤相关。问清患者平时状态及何处改变，再考虑病因。

00:13:13.224 --> 00:13:35.328
Observe work of breathing, speech, posture, mental status, skin, chest movement and sounds. Trend pulse, respirations, blood pressure and SpO2; use ECG or capnography when indicated and within your training. A treatment response can guide reassessment but does not prove a diagnosis.
观察呼吸功、言语、体位、意识、皮肤、胸廓运动及呼吸音。追踪脉搏、呼吸、血压和血氧；在有适应证且受训时使用ECG或二氧化碳监测。治疗反应可指导复评，却不能证明诊断。

00:13:35.328 --> 00:13:53.208
An adult reports sudden shortness of breath six days after knee surgery and several days of limited movement. The first observations are respiratory rate thirty-two, pulse one hundred twenty-two, oxygen saturation eighty-eight percent and systolic pressure eighty-six.
一名成人在膝关节手术6天后、数日活动减少，突然出现呼吸困难。初次观察：呼吸频率32、脉搏122、血氧88%、收缩压86。

00:13:53.208 --> 00:14:07.176
The history makes pulmonary embolism important to consider, but the observations do not prove it. Assess for other immediately dangerous causes while recognizing that hypotension and sudden onset indicate instability.
病史使肺栓塞成为重要考虑，但这些发现不能确诊。应同时评估其他紧急危险病因，并认识到低血压及突然发作提示不稳定。

00:14:07.176 --> 00:14:25.656
Use the current patient assessment and B06 pathway: support airway, oxygenation and ventilation as needed; obtain serial findings; arrange rapid conveyance and additional resources. Plan movement so that effective resuscitation remains possible.
按当前患者评估及B06路径处理：按需支持气道、氧合及通气；连续获取复评结果；安排快速转运及额外资源。规划搬动，确保仍可有效复苏。

00:14:25.656 --> 00:14:41.400
Do not delay conveyance to prove a diagnosis, apply an old score, start a video’s historical treatment or perform a procedure outside PCP scope. Give the receiving team the onset, risk factors, trends, support and response.
不要为了确诊、套用旧评分、实施视频中的历史治疗或执行PCP权限外操作而延误转运。应向接收团队交代发病时间、风险因素、趋势、支持措施及反应。

00:14:41.400 --> 00:14:56.208
First: the Queensland clip is a 2013 Australian service demonstration of a different device. Use only the current PR09 and the exact approved product instructions; continuous pressure does not replace a breath.
第一：昆士兰视频是2013年澳大利亚服务对另一种装置的演示。只能使用当前PR09及准确获批产品说明；持续压力不能代替一次通气。

00:14:56.208 --> 00:15:13.368
Second: PR27 describes a measured, marked, limited pharyngeal suction method. It is not gastric intubation or continuous suction; active vomiting calls for device removal, oropharyngeal clearance and restoration of support.
第二：PR27规定按尺寸测量、作标记且有限度的咽部吸引。它不是插胃管或持续吸引；活动性呕吐时须移除器械、清理口咽并恢复支持。

00:15:13.368 --> 00:15:27.864
Third: decreasing consciousness, respiratory rate or tidal volume suggests impending failure even if a previous saturation looked acceptable. Use the patient and trend, not one isolated number.
第三：意识、呼吸频率或潮气量下降提示即将衰竭，即使先前血氧看似可接受也一样。要看患者和趋势，不看单一数字。

00:15:27.864 --> 00:15:44.928
Fourth: recent surgery and immobility raise PE concern, but do not confirm PE. Reassess broadly, support the unstable patient, follow B06 and arrange rapid conveyance without importing historical US article treatment.
第四：近期手术及活动减少会提高对肺栓塞的警觉，但不能确诊。应广泛复评、支持不稳定患者、按B06快速转运，不照搬旧美国文章治疗。
